<section class="section-how-to-play" id="how-to-play">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header text-center">
      <span class="wood-badge">📜 Game Master Guide</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">How to Play Woody Sort Game</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">
        Learn the core rules and advanced strategic techniques to conquer even the most intricate Color Sort Puzzle layouts.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 Core Rules Cards -->
    <div class="rules-grid">
      <!-- Rule 1 -->
      <div class="woody-card rule-card">
        <div class="rule-badge">Rule 01</div>
        <div class="rule-icon">🎨</div>
        <h3 class="rule-title">Matching Top Ball Color</h3>
        <p class="rule-text">
          You can only move a ball into another wooden tube if that tube is either <strong>completely empty</strong> or its top ball is the <strong>exact same color</strong> as the ball you are moving.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Rule 2 -->
      <div class="woody-card rule-card">
        <div class="rule-badge">Rule 02</div>
        <div class="rule-icon">🧪</div>
        <h3 class="rule-title">Tube Capacity of 4</h3>
        <p class="rule-text">
          Each wooden tube holds a maximum of <strong>4 balls</strong>. You cannot pour a ball into a tube that is already at full capacity. Plan space wisely!
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Rule 3 -->
      <div class="woody-card rule-card">
        <div class="rule-badge">Rule 03</div>
        <div class="rule-icon">🏆</div>
        <h3 class="rule-title">Complete 4-of-a-Kind Tubes</h3>
        <p class="rule-text">
          The level is won when every color is gathered into its own dedicated tube of 4 matching balls, leaving the helper tubes cleanly empty.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Advanced Strategy Tips Box -->
    <div class="strategy-banner woody-card">
      <div class="strategy-header">
        <span class="strategy-icon">💡</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="strategy-title">Master Strategy: 4 Pro Tips for Winning</h3>
          <p class="strategy-subtitle">Techniques used by top color sort puzzle champions</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="strategy-points-grid">
        <div class="strat-point">
          <strong>1. Protect Your Empty Tubes:</strong> An empty tube is your most precious resource. Don't fill it with random colors unless you have a clear combo move to empty another tube.
        </div>
        <div class="strat-point">
          <strong>2. Uncover Buried Colors:</strong> Focus your moves on liberating colors trapped beneath mismatched balls, rather than randomly shuffling matching pairs.
        </div>
        <div class="strat-point">
          <strong>3. Leverage Cascading Pours:</strong> In Woody Sort, moving multiple identical balls in a single cascade saves time and clears bottleneck stacks faster.
        </div>
        <div class="strat-point">
          <strong>4. Use the +1 Tube Booster:</strong> If a layout seems deadlocked, trigger the auxiliary wooden tube booster to provide crucial extra breathing room!
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section-how-to-play {
    padding: 60px 0;
  }

  .text-center {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 12px 0 8px;
  }

  .section-desc {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .rules-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .rule-card {
    position: relative;
    padding-top: 36px;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .rule-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    border-color: var(--wood-gold);
  }

  .rule-badge {
    position: absolute;
    top: 16px;
    right: 18px;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--wood-gold);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .rule-icon {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .rule-title {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--wood-gold-light);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .rule-text {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .rule-text strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* Strategy Banner */
  .strategy-banner {
    border: 2px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.4);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(61, 35, 20, 0.95) 0%, rgba(32, 19, 9, 0.95) 100%);
  }

  .strategy-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.25);
    padding-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .strategy-icon {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
  }

  .strategy-title {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--wood-gold);
  }

  .strategy-subtitle {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .strategy-points-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
  }

  .strat-point {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    background: rgba(26, 18, 11, 0.6);
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15);
  }

  .strat-point strong {
    color: var(--wood-gold-light);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .rules-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .strategy-points-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
